        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a1bcda43-9801-57f2-bd8c-d11cf242488f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Electoral district of Bass, Pakenham, Melbourne, Inverloch, Phillip Island, Victoria, Australia\n- Organizations: Victorian Legislative Assembly, Liberal Party of Australia, Shire of Cardinia\n- People: Brian Paynter\n- Topics: electoral geography, political representation\n\nFacts:\n- The Electoral district of Bass covers 1,383 square kilometres south-east of Melbourne, extending from outer suburban Pakenham through rural areas to the coast at Inverloch and Phillip Island.\n- The Electoral district of Bass includes Bass, Cape Paterson, Corinella, Cowes, Grantville, Inverloch, Kilcunda, Koo Wee Rup, Lang Lang, Rhyll, San Remo, Ventnor, Wonthaggi, and part of suburban Pakenham.\n- Pakenham is a satellite suburb of Melbourne in Victoria, Australia, on the edge of the West Gippsland region and 56 kilometres south-east of Melbourne's Central Business District.\n- Pakenham is located within the Shire of Cardinia local government area.\n- Since November 2014, Brian Paynter has been the Liberal Party of Australia member of the Victorian Legislative Assembly for the seat of Bass.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d250a74f-9c3f-50f2-a0fc-53a2346b7998",
        "text": "Page: Electoral district of Bass. Sentence: It covers an area of 1,383 sqkm south east of Melbourne, stretching from outer suburban Pakenham through rural areas to the coast at Inverloch and Phillip Island.\nPage: Electoral district of Bass. Sentence: It includes the towns of Bass, Cape Patterson, Corinella, Cowes, Grantville, Inverloch, Kilcunda, Koo Wee Rup, Lang Lang, Rhyll, San Remo, Ventnor, Wonthaggi, and part of suburban Pakenham.\nPage: Pakenham, Victoria. Sentence: Pakenham is a satellite suburb of Melbourne on the edge of the West Gippsland region of Victoria, Australia, 56 km south-east of Melbourne's Central Business District, located within the Shire of Cardinia local government area.\nPage: Brian Paynter. Sentence: He has been a Liberal Party of Australia member of the Victorian Legislative Assembly since November 2014, representing the Legislative Assembly seat of Bass.",
